## 7. The central limit theorem

Set the seed with `set.seed(343)`. Use `sample()` to draw a random sub-sample of 10 plants from `SI`, then one of 100, then one of 500. For each sub-sample report the mean, the standard deviation and the width of the 95% confidence interval (upper limit minus lower limit), and compare them with the values for all 866 SI plants from Sections 4 and 6.

```{r clt}
set.seed(343)

# Draw random subsamples from SI
sub_10 = sample(SI, size=10)
sub_100 = sample(SI, size=100)
sub_500 = sample(SI, size=500)


# sub_10 calculations
sub_10_samplesize = length(sub_10)
sub_10_mean = mean(sub_10)
sub_10_sd = sd(sub_10)
sub_10_se = sub_10_sd/ sqrt(sub_10_samplesize)
sub_10_ciwidth = 2 * 1.96 *sub_10_se

# sub_100 calculations
sub_100_samplesize = length(sub_100)
sub_100_mean = mean(sub_100)
sub_100_sd = sd(sub_100)
sub_100_se = sub_100_sd/ sqrt(sub_100_samplesize)
sub_100_ciwidth = 2 * 1.96 *sub_100_se

# sub_500 calculations
sub_500_samplesize = length(sub_500)
sub_500_mean = mean(sub_500)
sub_500_sd = sd(sub_500)
sub_500_se = sub_500_sd/ sqrt(sub_500_samplesize)
sub_500_ciwidth = 2 * 1.96 *sub_500_se
# CI <- c(x - 1.96 * se, x + 1.96 * se)
# CI[2] - CI[1]   # RSCC’s example


# full vector calculations
SI_samplesize = length(SI)
SI_mean = mean(SI)
SI_sd = sd(SI)
SI_se = SI_sd/ sqrt(SI_samplesize)
SI_ciwidth = 2 * 1.96 *SI_se

# Comparison & Printing results out
SI_comparison = data.frame(
    Sample = c("Subsample 10", "Subsample 100", "Subsample 500", "Full SI Sample"),
    Sample_Size = c(sub_10_samplesize, sub_100_samplesize, sub_500_samplesize, SI_samplesize),
    Mean = c(sub_10_mean, sub_100_mean, sub_500_mean, SI_mean),
    SD = c(sub_10_sd, sub_100_sd, sub_500_sd, SI_sd),
    CI_Width = c(sub_10_ciwidth, sub_100_ciwidth, sub_500_ciwidth, SI_ciwidth)
)

print(SI_comparison)

```

