# Part 4 — Probability and tests

## 8. Z-scores and probability

Convert `SI` to z-scores and plot a histogram of them. Then convert the **mean of the SC plants** to a z-score relative to the SI sample (subtract the SI mean, divide by the SI standard deviation), and use `pnorm()` to calculate the probability of drawing a plant with a face diameter that small **or smaller** from the SI population.

```{r z-scores, message=FALSE}

# Convert SI values to z-scores
SI_z=(SI-mean(SI)) / sd(SI)

# Plot histogram of SI z-scores
ggplot(data.frame(z=SI_z), aes(x=z)) + 
    geom_histogram(binwidth=0.25,      colour="black", fill="skyblue") + 
    labs(
        x = "Z-score", 
        y = "Count", 
        title = "Distribution of SI face Diameter Z-scores"
    ) + 
    theme_classic()
    
# Calculate SC mean z-score relative to SI population
SC_mean=mean(SC)
z_SC_mean = (SC_mean - mean(SI)/ sd(SI))

# Calculate thbe probability of drawing a plant with a diameter this small or smaller 
p_value=pnorm(z_SC_mean)

# print results
print(z_SC_mean)
print(p_value)

```

**Question 7:** Is this a one-tailed or a two-tailed question, and why? What does the probability say about whether SC flowers are simply small SI flowers?

**Answer:**

## 9. Two-sample *t*-test

Test whether SI and SC plants differ in face diameter with a t-test. Report *t*, the degrees of freedom, the p-value and the 95% confidence interval of the difference. Then calculate *t* yourself from the two-sample equation, $t = (\bar x - \bar y) / \sqrt{SE_x^2 + SE_y^2}$, using the standard errors from Section 6, and check that it matches.

```{r t-test}

# standard two-sample t-test
t_test_result=t.test(SI, SC)
print(t_test_result)

# Extract key test metrics
t_val = t_test_result$statistic
df_val = t_test_result$parameter
p_val = t_test_result$p.value
ci_diff = t_test_result$conf.int

# summarize and print the results

# Manual calculations to ensure there is no errors
SC_samplesize = length(SC)
SC_sd = sd(SC)
se_SC = SC_sd/ sqrt(SC_samplesize)

t_manual = (mean_SI - mean_SC) / sqrt(se_SI^2 + se_SC^2)

# summarize and print the results again
t_summary = data.frame(
    Metric = c("t-statistic", "Degrees of Freedom (df)", "p-value", "95% CI Lower", "95% CI Upper"),
    R_t.test = c(t_val, df_val, p_val, ci_diff[1], ci_diff[2] ),
    Manual = c(t_manual, "NA", "NA", "NA", "NA")
)
print(t_summary)

```

